{"id":"1907400677073852024","kind":"article","title":"反对双重思想","author":"Rob Bensinger","original_authors":["Rob Bensinger"],"original_source_urls":["https://www.readthesequences.com/Against-Doublethink-Sequence"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"理性 & 克服偏见","date":"2025-05-18","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":32,"comment_count":2,"minutes":1,"chars":420,"keywords":["双重思想","事后合理化","自我欺骗","认知偏差","反思"],"summary":"本文作为《反对双重思想》系列导读，指出人们常把事后编造的连贯故事误当成提升准确性的推理，并链接到关于自我欺骗、偏见和反思的后续文章。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/1907400677073852024","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"4MEH1sA1\">这场达特茅斯-普林斯顿的比赛给我们带来一个启示：我们的大部分推理过程实际上是在事后合理化——我们编造故事，让自己当前的观点显得更加连贯和有道理，但这并不一定能提高观点的准确性。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Against-Rationalization-Sequence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《反对合理化》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>系列探讨了这一问题，而<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Against-Doublethink-Sequence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《反对双重思想》</a>（关于自我欺骗）和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Seeing-With-Fresh-Eyes-Sequence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《用新眼光看问题》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>（关于挑战我们识别与预期和假设不符的证据的能力）系列则对此进行了进一步阐述。</p><p data-pid=\"Ud4DoIGV\">——<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Rationality-An-Introduction\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《理性：序言》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>by Rob Bensinger</p><hr/><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"30666103864\" href=\"#/post/30666103864\">单重思想</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"32609362607\" href=\"#/post/32609362607\">双重思想（选择带有偏见）</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1888562465278760704\" href=\"#/post/1888562465278760704\">不，真的，我欺骗了自己</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm